@startuml Clustering_Model_Lifecycle
!theme plain
title Clustering Model Lifecycle Management

state "Model Not Exists" as NotExists
state "Model Training" as Training
state "Model Active" as Active
state "Model Retraining" as Retraining
state "Model Expired" as Expired

state Training {
    state "Load Vectors" as LoadVectors
    state "K-means++ Init" as KMeansInit
    state "Iterative Refinement" as Refinement
    state "Model Persistence" as Persistence
    state "Statistics Calculation" as StatsCalc
    
    LoadVectors --> KMeansInit
    KMeansInit --> Refinement
    Refinement --> StatsCalc
    StatsCalc --> Persistence
}

state Active {
    state "Serving Searches" as ServingSearches
    state "Monitoring Growth" as MonitoringGrowth
    state "Model Validation" as ModelValidation
    
    ServingSearches --> MonitoringGrowth
    MonitoringGrowth --> ModelValidation
    ModelValidation --> ServingSearches
}

state Retraining {
    state "Background Training" as BackgroundTraining
    state "Model Comparison" as ModelComparison
    state "Atomic Replacement" as AtomicReplacement
    
    BackgroundTraining --> ModelComparison
    ModelComparison --> AtomicReplacement
}

' Transitions
NotExists --> Training : Collection reaches\n1M vectors
Training --> Active : Training completes\nsuccessfully
Active --> Retraining : 20% growth threshold\nreached
Retraining --> Active : New model deployed
Active --> Expired : Collection deleted\nor size < 1M
Expired --> NotExists : Cleanup complete

Training --> NotExists : Training fails
Retraining --> Active : Retraining fails\n(keep old model)

' Transition conditions and actions
NotExists : **Condition**: Collection vector count < 1M
NotExists : **Action**: Use direct search only

Training : **Trigger**: BackgroundManager detects 1M+ vectors
Training : **Process**: 
Training : - Load all vectors from storage
Training : - Apply K-means++ initialization
Training : - Iterative centroid refinement
Training : - Calculate model statistics
Training : - Persist to __models/ directory
Training : **Duration**: 30-300 seconds depending on collection size

Active : **Condition**: Valid model exists and collection > 1M vectors
Active : **Capabilities**:
Active : - Cluster-optimized search available
Active : - Parallel cluster processing
Active : - 3-5x storage efficiency
Active : - Continuous growth monitoring
Active : **Monitoring**: Track vector count growth for retraining threshold

Retraining : **Trigger**: Current vector count >= 1.20 * last_training_count
Retraining : **Strategy**: 
Retraining : - Train new model in background
Retraining : - Compare performance with current model
Retraining : - Atomic replacement if improvement detected
Retraining : - Fallback to old model if training fails
Retraining : **Coordination**: Scheduled with flush/compaction cycles

Expired : **Triggers**:
Expired : - Collection deleted
Expired : - Vector count drops below 1M
Expired : - Model corruption detected
Expired : **Cleanup**:
Expired : - Remove model files from __models/
Expired : - Clear statistics
Expired : - Revert to direct search

note top of Training
    **Training Performance:**
    - 1M vectors: ~30-60 seconds
    - 10M vectors: ~2-5 minutes
    - 100M vectors: ~10-30 minutes
    - Parallel processing available
    - SIMD optimizations enabled
end note

note top of Active
    **Model Statistics Tracked:**
    - Vector count at training time
    - Cluster count and distribution
    - Training duration and timestamp
    - Inertia and silhouette scores
    - Search performance metrics
end note

note top of Retraining
    **Retraining Optimization:**
    - Only triggered at 20% growth
    - Background training prevents disruption
    - Atomic model replacement
    - Performance comparison validation
    - Graceful degradation on failure
end note

@enduml